-- statement:
--   This bundle defines the question reindexings and operator families for the commute-G-half-sandwich comparison. Its constructions expose the head, tail, moved, and commuted endpoints and provide the equivalences needed to add one move to the chain.
--
--   Principal definitions:
--   - `pointTupleConsEquiv`: the equivalence that splits a nonempty tuple of slice questions into its first point and remaining tail.
--   - `gHatReverseHalfProductOutcomeOperator`: the reverse-ordered half-product of completed-slice outcome operators.
--   - `headTailOrderedFamily`: the ordered head-tail family with the head factor first on the left register.
--   - `headTailRotatedFamily`: the rotated family with the tail half-product preceding the head factor.
--   - `commuteGHalfSandwich_moveFamily`: the move-family endpoint with distinguished factors on opposite tensor registers.
--   - `commuteGHalfSandwich_commuteFamily`: the endpoint obtained by commuting the two distinguished left-register factors.
--   - `thirdSliceFrontEquiv`: the equivalence that moves a third distinguished slice coordinate to the front.
--   - `splitQuestionEquiv`: the reassociation equivalence from a head-tail question and one added slice to a move-chain question.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
